.TH ECHO 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
echo \- echo arguments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echo
.RB [ \-n ]
.RI [ arg ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Echo
writes its arguments in order as a line on the standard output file.
It is mainly useful for producing diagnostics in command files.
Arguments are separated by one space.
An initial, separate
.B \-n
suppresses the final newline.
Backslash escapes are not interpreted.
